{"type":"block","data":{"id":"adoctext1000000000000000000","parentId":"adoccard1000000000000000000","rootId":"bdoc00000000000000000000000","createdBy":"system","modifiedBy":"system","schema":1,"type":"text","title":"## How this works\n\n1. Set up a folder for the agent to work in — the app asks for one when the board is set up.\n2. Make a card and describe the task in it the way you would explain it to a person: what is needed, and how to tell it is done.\n3. Drag it into the «Agent writes» column — an agent picks it up, and a terminal button appears on the card: it shows what the agent is doing, and it is where you talk to it.\n4. When it finishes, the card travels on along its route by itself. What it did, it says in that same terminal.\n\nThis card can be deleted — it starts nothing.\n\nThe folder for this board is the documentation repository. The agent writes on a branch of its own per card: nothing changes on the main branch until you merge it, and the branch name is on the card.","fields":{},"createAt":1785888000000,"updateAt":1785888000000,"deleteAt":0}}
